 ],
 "literal": "Even touching, will it be possible, I wonder? Excellent / bow-possessing whistling hunters, throwing stones, roused / in the wide forest, separated from its herd, / a distressed innocent deer, when it appeared before them, her brothers / with swift force from their excellent bows, pierced the chest of a stag, / and pulled out with blood, the red-shafted arrow / like which are the fighting kohl-adorned eyes / of the mountain girl with fragrant dark hair, her shoulders!",
 "translation": "Will it ever be possible for me to even touch the shoulders of this mountain girl with fragrant dark hair? Her kohl-adorned eyes, striking and sharp, are like the red-shafted arrow pulled out, dripping with blood, from the chest of a stag—pierced with swift force from an excellent bow by her brothers, when they encountered a distressed, innocent deer that had been separated from its herd in the wide forest, roused by whistling hunters throwing stones with their bows.",
 "modern": "கல் எறிந்து விலங்குகளை எழுப்பும் வில் ஏந்திய வேடர்கள், அகன்ற காட்டில் தன் கூட்டத்திலிருந்து பிரிந்து வருந்தும் இளமையான பெண் மானை விரட்ட, அது தன் முன்னே வர, அவளுடைய அண்ணன்மார்கள் சிறந்த வில்லிலிருந்து வீசிய வேகமான அம்பினை ஆண் மானின் மார்பில் பாய்ச்சி, குருதியோடு பிடுங்கிய செங்கோல் அம்பு போன்ற போரிடும் மை தீட்டிய கண்களையும், நறுமணமுள்ள கரிய கூந்தலையும் உடைய குறிஞ்சி நிலப் பெண்ணின் தோள்களைத் தொடுவதற்காவது எனக்கு வாய்ப்புக் கிடைக்குமா?",
 "explanation": "The hero speaks to himself after encountering the heroine in the mountain slopes. He is deeply struck by her beauty, particularly her sharp, kohl-adorned eyes, which he compares to a bloody, red-shafted arrow. He describes a hunting scene where whistling hunters rouse an innocent deer separated from its herd, and the heroine's brothers shoot a stag with swift force, pulling out the bloody arrow. Her eyes are as sharp, red-streaked, and piercing as that very arrow, yet they captivate him completely. He wonders longingly if he will ever be fortunate enough to even touch her beautiful shoulders. This intense imagery of the hunt and the sharp arrow perfectly reflects the Kuriñci landscape, where love is sudden, piercing, and deeply felt.",
